      "math_academy_id": "q-174376",
      "sequence_position": 2,
      "problem": "Which of the following is the indicator function ${1}_{A}(x)$ of the subset $A=\\{1,2\\}$ of $X=\\{-2,-1,0,1,2\\}.$",
      "worked_solution": "An indicator function maps elements from a set to the values $0$ or $1,$ depending on whether the element belongs to a specified subset. The indicator function is designed to \"indicate\" whether an element is a member of a subset.\n\nMore specifically, consider a universal set $X.$ Then, the indicator function of a set $A⊆X$ is the function\n\n$$\n{1}_{A}(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}1, & \\text{if }x\\in A, \\\\ 0, & \\text{if }x\\notin A.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe indicator function of the set $\\{1,2\\}$ is shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14274148/assets/4ccd0aab0a3e67bfed1fe90f4868b374fb9e443da559aa3cc34b4033c7e40427.png)\n\n \n\nNotice that the elements $1$ and $2$ (the elements of our subset) are mapped to $1,$ and all other elements are mapped to $0.$",
